+// gmstream (0008): throttle a FIFO game instead of queueing its frames. Without
+// this a game is released when a frame is shown, runs ahead by its frame
+// latency, and that many finished frames wait here for good if it makes them
+// as fast as we show them. So presented events are held and let go one per
+// refresh: the game starts a frame when it can be shown next, and reads its
+// input as late as it can. While frames still wait, one release is skipped, so
+// the backlog drains without dropping any. With no queue a frame's phase
+// decides everything: done just after a latch it waits a whole refresh. So each
+// release is nudged until frames are done k_ulGmThrottleLeadNs before the latch.
+gamescope::ConVar<bool> cv_gm_throttle( "gm_throttle", true, "Throttle FIFO games instead of queueing their frames." );
+static constexpr uint64_t k_ulGmThrottleLeadNs = 2'000'000;
+// How long the window's last frame was done before it was latched.
+static std::unordered_map<uint64_t, uint64_t> s_GmThrottleWait;
+
